# Build context for the images under docker/.
#
# The Maven build inside the image needs the poms, the Java sources and the resources. It
# regenerates everything else — the studio's frontend assets and every target/ directory —
# so none of it travels, and a stale artifact from the host could only mean an image that
# ships something its own build did not produce.
#
# What is deliberately NOT excluded is the shipped product: smith-common/ and prod/. The
# POC tree below poc/ is frozen evidence behind the `poc` Maven profile, which the image
# builds never enable, so its sources are dead weight in a layer.

# Version control and the local clone of the remote
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Build output — regenerated inside the image
target/
**/target/
*.class
*.jar

# The studio frontend's toolchain and output. frontend-maven-plugin installs its own Node and
# `npm run build` regenerates src/main/resources/static (both are gitignored for exactly this
# reason), so a host-built bundle must not ride along.
**/node_modules/
**/frontend/.quasar/
**/frontend/node/
prod/embabel-smith-studio/src/main/resources/static/

# Developer-local configuration. application-local.yaml is gitignored and names the dev
# Postgres endpoint and its credentials; a packaged run is meant to set its own profile, and
# an image that inherited a developer's file would boot against a database nobody intended.
application-local.yaml
**/application-local.yaml
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Repositories and trees no shipped module reads
poc/
built-specs/
graphify-out/
.wiki/
.wiki-*/
docs/
examples/
openspec/
.tmp/
.tmp-qwen/
.qwen/
.agents/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.jbeval/
.pi/
.poc-runs/
node/

# Frozen evidence and scratch
*.log
*.zip
skills-lock.json
run-loop.sh
